 (CK) levels to prevent serious complications.**\n\n**Memory hook:** Remember: CK for **C**ritical **K**onnection to muscle health in statin therapy.","kind":"delete_generic+dup"},{"id":"cmqw6318p001k1ypotbtvevm7","old_md5":"acd15a3303400fc95251fb734f779c63","expl":"## Why this answer is correct\nThe pharmacist should emphasize the risk of sexual dysfunction with sertraline.\n• **Sexual dysfunction** is a well-documented side effect of SSRIs like sertraline.\n• This side effect can significantly impact **quality of life** and adherence to treatment.\n• While other side effects exist, sexual dysfunction is often more prevalent and concerning for patients.\n**In practice:** In practice, this means that addressing sexual side effects can help patients feel more comfortable and engaged in their treatment plan, potentially improving adherence and outcomes.\n## Why the other options are wrong\n\n\n\n**Risk of serotonin syndrome.**\n• Trap: Students may think serotonin syndrome is a common side effect of SSRIs.\n• Why it fails here: Serotonin syndrome is a serious but rare condition typically associated with drug interactions or overdose, not common use of sertraline.\n• Remember: Understanding the relative frequency of side effects is crucial for effective patient counseling.\n\n**Risk of weight gain.**\n• Trap: Some may believe that weight gain is a primary concern with SSRIs.\n• Why it fails here: While weight gain can occur with long-term use of SSRIs, it is not as prevalent as sexual dysfunction, especially in the early stages of treatment.\n• Remember: Recognizing the most common side effects helps prioritize patient education.\n\n**Risk of drowsiness.**\n• Trap: Students might assume that drowsiness is a significant side effect of all antidepressants.\n• Why it fails here: Drowsiness can occur but is not a primary concern with sertraline compared to sexual dysfunction, which is more frequently reported.\n• Remember: Focusing on the most impactful side effects ensure