ay believe that changing corticosteroids will provide better control.\n• Why it fails here: This option fails here because the current combination inhaler with fluticasone and salmeterol is already effective, and switching corticosteroids does not address the need for additional bronchodilation.\n• Remember: Effective management of COPD often requires adding different classes of medications rather than just switching within one class.\n\n**Add a leukotriene receptor antagonist**\n• Trap: Students might think leukotriene receptor antagonists are beneficial for COPD management.\n• Why it fails here: This fails for this patient because leukotriene receptor antagonists are primarily used for asthma and do not provide the necessary bronchodilation needed in COPD.\n• Remember: Understanding the specific roles of different medication classes is crucial in managing COPD effectively.\n## Key takeaway\n**When managing COPD, prioritize adding a long-acting bronchodilator like tiotropium over increasing doses or switching medications.**\n\n**Memory hook:** Think LAMA for COPD: Long-Acting Muscarinic Antagonists are key!","kind":"lead_in+dup"},{"id":"cmr08ae1s00541y3sfasvrrt9","old_md5":"a8ff05262ef7fec22f95da9a7843055d","expl":"## Why this answer is correct\nRemaining upright for at least 30 minutes after taking alendronate is essential to prevent esophageal irritation.\n• **Alendronate** is a bisphosphonate used to treat osteoporosis.\n• It can cause **esophageal irritation** if the patient lies down immediately after taking it.\n• Proper administration enhances **absorption** and minimizes side effects.\n## Why the other options are wrong\n\n\n\n**Take the medication with food to enhance absorption.**\n• Trap: Students may think that food can help with absorption.\n• Why it fails here: In reality, food significantly decreases the absorption of alendronate, making this advice harmful.\n• Remember: Understanding the proper administration of medications is crucial for their effe